{
  "schema": "mycelix-tcdm-transition-contract-v1",
  "profile": "FailClosedTCDMTransitionCandidateV1",
  "status": "research-only candidate transition semantics; not production behavior",
  "decision_rules": [
    "All input trust_level and confidence values must be finite and in [0,1]; decay_rate must be finite and in [0,1]; interaction_count must fit u32.",
    "When last_update is the existing zero sentinel, the first valid decay call initializes the watermark and applies no decay.",
    "For an initialized state, timestamps must be monotone nondecreasing; backward time or checked i64 subtraction overflow rejects without mutation.",
    "For a valid positive elapsed duration, trust decays by decay_rate^(elapsed_seconds/86400), confidence by the square root of that factor; equal timestamps produce no decay.",
    "Decay rate zero means immediate zero after positive elapsed time; decay rate one means no decay.",
    "Interaction weight must be finite and nonnegative. Positive weights are capped at 0.3; confidence grows by 0.05*(effective_weight/0.3), clamped to [0,1]. Accepted positive-weight interactions increment the u32 count with checked arithmetic.",
    "Zero interaction weight means no evidence: state and count are unchanged and confidence must not increase.",
    "Any invalid state or input rejects without committing a partial state update."
  ],
